                "headline": "Special Weather Statement issued October 21 at 6:45AM MDT by NWS Goodland KS",
                "description": "Patchy dense fog continues in the Kansas and Nebraska border area.\nMcCook and Oberlin have recently reported visibility as low as a\nquarter of a mile. The fog will continue for another few hours\nbefore burning off between 10 and 11 AM CDT.\n\nWildlife, stalled vehicles and other road obstructions will be\ndifficult to spot. Low visibility may cause the time to slow down\nand stop to be longer than the time you are able to see ahead.",
